    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for May 27th is anchored by **Andy Pages**, who stands as our strongest play with a 72.80 score. Facing Sugano (4.79 xERA), **Andy Pages** benefits from a favorable matchup and a deliberate pitcher delivery that yields a projected 88% success rate for potential stolen base attempts\u2014a critical variable given our focus on the scarcest category. Alongside him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (66.74) and **Gunnar Henderson** (62.64) provide elite stability in the #2 hole. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** are particularly intriguing; despite facing a lefty in Matz, both receive a +16% park factor bump that helps overcome the neutral platoon disadvantage, keeping them firmly in the \"Strong\" start category.\n\nStrategic benching remains essential for managing our game-cap efficiency, as evidenced by our decision to hold **Jackson Merrill** (39.03) and **Josh Jung** (50.89) in reserve. While **Josh Jung** posted a respectable score, he was squeezed out by the deeper lineup context and efficiency of our starters. The most difficult decision was pivoting away from **Jackson Merrill**; although he is a core piece of our future, the combination of an elite matchup against S\u00e1nchez (2.88 xERA) and the catcher\u2019s quick pop-time profile dropped his projected efficiency below our 40-point floor. We are monitoring **Sam Antonacci** (41.73) closely, as his lopsided L/L platoon disadvantage against Prielipp nearly pushed him to the bench as well. Owners should note that **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, and with **Kyle Tucker** out of the lineup today, we must rely on the current configuration to maximize our 5x5 output.",
